# Scratch output from tools/wholesale_scan.py and the Keepa/sourcing tooling —
# regenerable by re-running against the supplier feeds, not source. Since
# 2026-09-09 every scanned product is also persisted to supplier_scan_results
# (see app/models.py); the .jsonl checkpoints remain the resume mechanism and
# tools/backfill_scan_results.py can replay them.
*_stage1_checkpoint.jsonl
*_stage2_checkpoint.jsonl
*_candidates.txt
*_candidates_limited.txt
candidates_*.txt
*_scan.log
*_scan_checkpoint.jsonl
*_scan_scored.txt
*_recovered_eans.json
*_matching_asins.json
sourcing_data.json
sourcing_channels.json
sourcing_list.txt

# Supplier feeds that a tool regenerates. vp_feed.csv is deliberately NOT
# ignored: it was transcribed by hand from a PDF-style price list and there
# is no scraper that can rebuild it.
data/*
!data/vp_feed.csv
